The exhaustive search finds every critical point without seeding, and was
validated against Duistermaat's four-mode window. Where the two disagree,
the midpoint-seeded count is the one at fault: seeding at the midpoint of a
far-apart pair converges to a saddle that belongs to a different pair, and
a 1e-5 dedup tolerance then counts it twice.
